.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "Version 0.4.1" "myutils Library"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a substring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "#include \(dqmyfilefunctions.h\(dq"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR mygrep ()
function scans every line of the file stream pointed to by
.I fp
for occurrences of the substring
.IR search_str .
It allocates
.I *matches
as a dynamically growing array of dynamically allocated strings, one per
matching line, with the trailing newline stripped.
.PP
The caller is responsible for freeing each string in
.I *matches
and then freeing
.I *matches
itself once done.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the number of matching lines found is returned (which may be
zero). Returns \-1 if
.IR fp ", " search_str ", or " matches
is NULL, or if memory allocation fails.
.SH AUTHOR
Husnain Raza <husnain@example.com>
